{"id":4390,"date":"2021-12-06T15:20:18","date_gmt":"2021-12-06T23:20:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=4390"},"modified":"2025-09-02T09:06:41","modified_gmt":"2025-09-02T16:06:41","slug":"4-2-user-input-controller-cde","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/4-2-user-input-controller-cde\/","title":{"rendered":"4.2: Keyboard Controller"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c1968ae\" name=\"6a2213c1968ae\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Before You Fly<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1730227373096{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>PRE-FLIGHT WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise caution while piloting your drone. To prolong the longevity of your drone, avoid flying into walls or other objects. Prior to takeoff, please review lesson <em>0.2 \u201cBefore You Fly\u201d.<\/em><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c1969fd\" name=\"6a2213c1969fd\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Goals and Steps to Success<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1724801149531{padding-top: 15px !important;padding-right: 15px !important;padding-bottom: 15px !important;padding-left: 15px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-11930 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/06\/product_brand-300x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"85\" data-wp-editing=\"1\" srcset=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/06\/product_brand-300x85.png 300w, https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/06\/product_brand.png 729w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em>This lesson currently is not optimized for \u201cPython for Robolink\u201d. Results may vary for console input functions.<\/em><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]Goals:<\/p>\n<p>By the end of this lesson, I will be able to:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Identify the importance of input in programs<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Create and run programs that include user interaction<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Store and modify user inputs<\/span><\/li>\n<li>Utilize user input to make decisions in a program<\/li>\n<li>Allow user input to change program flow during flight<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Steps to Success:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Controller<\/li>\n<li>Takeoff<\/li>\n<li>While Loop<\/li>\n<li>Making Decisions<\/li>\n<li>Challenge: Super Program<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196a78\" name=\"6a2213c196a78\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Keyboard Controller<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">User input is also great for controlling your drone! In this activity, you will program your keyboard to act as a controller, with \u201cW-A-S-D\u201d and \u201cI-J-K-L\u201d keys as the joysticks.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7994&#8243; img_size=&#8221;640&#215;543&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">First, import the \u201ctime\u201d library. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Next, show a menu of \u201c<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Command options<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201d and assign a key to each of the eight flight directions: positive and negative roll, pitch, yaw, and throttle. Make sure to include a \u201c<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">quit<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201d option, which will land the drone.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your menu should look something like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">from codrone_edu.drone import *\r\nimport time\r\n\r\ndrone = Drone()\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\"Command Options: \")\r\nprint(\"\"\"w: throttle up\r\ns: throttle down\r\na: yaw left\r\nd: yaw right\r\ni: pitch forward\r\nk: pitch backward\r\nj: roll left\r\nl: roll right\r\nq: quit\"\"\")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196ad9\" name=\"6a2213c196ad9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Takeoff<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Have your drone take off, and then set your trim if needed. This is for if your drone is drifting, and you want to fix its pitch or roll.\u00a0 If you\u2019re not having that issue, you can skip this step.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Next, create a variable called <strong>power<\/strong> and set its value to 40. This way, the default power will be 40%.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your code should look like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">drone.takeoff()\r\n\r\npower = 40<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196b44\" name=\"6a2213c196b44\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>While Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Set up a while loop so that while true, the program can take user input to make decisions. Next, reset the roll, pitch, yaw, and throttle to 0.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Create a variable called <\/span><strong>direction<\/strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to store <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">input()<\/code><\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. In the parameters for <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">input()<\/code><\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">write<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u201cInput a command: \u201d. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This will print the command, and when the user inputs a letter, it will be stored as an option and called later on.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your code should look like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">while True:\r\n\r\n    drone.set_throttle(0)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_roll(0)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_yaw(0)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_pitch(0)\r\n\r\n    drone.move(0.5)\r\n\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 direction = input(\"Input a command: \")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196bd0\" name=\"6a2213c196bd0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Making Decisions<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Just like the user input menu, you need to use if, else if, and else statements to have your drone fly in different directions based on the user input. For the \u201cw\u201d key, use an if statement and then include a command for your drone to throttle up. In the parameters, use the <strong>power<\/strong> variable, which will have the drone move at 40% power.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">    if direction == \"w\":\r\n\r\n        drone.set_throttle(power)<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For the other 7 flight commands, use else if statements. If you want the drone to go to the left, down, or backwards, put a negative sign next to the<strong> power<\/strong> variable in the parameters.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">elif direction == \"s\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_throttle(-power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"a\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_yaw(-power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"d\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_yaw(power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"i\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_pitch(power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"k\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_pitch(-power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"j\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_roll(-power)\r\n\r\nelif direction == \"l\":\r\n\r\n    drone.set_roll(power)<\/pre>\n<p>Write one more else if statement for the quit option. Add a wait, so the landing command isn\u2019t skipped. Next, land the drone and break out of the loop.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">    elif direction == \"q\":\r\n       time.sleep(1)\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0drone.land()\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0break<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Include an option that will let the user know they made a mistake if they input something that isn\u2019t an option in the program.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">    else:\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0    print(\"Not a command\")<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Finally, include a move command for one second. This is what will actually move the drone, along with the code you wrote for each key!<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">  drone.move(1)<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Outside the loop, include a print command so you know when you\u2019ve exited the program.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">print(\"Done\")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196c28\" name=\"6a2213c196c28\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final Code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">from codrone_edu.drone import *\r\nimport time\r\n\r\ndrone = Drone()\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\"Command Options: \")\r\nprint(\"\"\"w: throttle up\r\ns: throttle down\r\na: yaw left\r\nd: yaw right\r\ni: pitch forward\r\nk: pitch backward\r\nj: roll left\r\nl: roll right\r\nq: quit\"\"\")\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\npower = 40\r\n\r\nwhile True:\r\n    drone.set_throttle(0)\r\n    drone.set_roll(0)\r\n    drone.set_yaw(0)\r\n    drone.set_pitch(0)\r\n\r\n    drone.move(0.5)\r\n\r\n    direction = input(\"Input a command: \")\r\n\r\n    if direction == \"w\":\r\n        drone.set_throttle(power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"s\":\r\n        drone.set_throttle(-power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"a\":\r\n        drone.set_yaw(-power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"d\":\r\n        drone.set_yaw(power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"i\":\r\n        drone.set_pitch(power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"k\":\r\n        drone.set_pitch(-power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"j\":\r\n        drone.set_roll(-power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"l\":\r\n        drone.set_roll(power)\r\n\r\n    elif direction == \"q\":\r\n        time.sleep(1)\r\n        drone.land()\r\n        break\r\n\r\n    else:\r\n        print(\"Not a command\")\r\n\r\n    drone.move(1)\r\nprint(\"Done\")\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196c89\" name=\"6a2213c196c89\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge: Super Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_single_image image=&#8221;8001&#8243; img_size=&#8221;720&#215;405&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">So you have a program that uses numbers to have your CoDrone EDU do different maneuvers, and you have another program that uses letters to have your CoDrone EDU fly in different directions. <em>What if you combined them both in the same program?<\/em><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rules:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Must include an option to quit<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Must include a print command that lets the user know when they input an option that\u2019s not available<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213c196cd0\" name=\"6a2213c196cd0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned about user input! User input can be used to allow the user to decide the outcome of a program, and in this case you wrote a program to allow the user to control the CoDrone EDU using their keyboard.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7546&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Before You Fly [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1730227373096{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] PRE-FLIGHT WARNING Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise caution while piloting your drone. To prolong&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/4-2-user-input-controller-cde\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":10822,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3875,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,4328,14401,2119,2121,2122,2134,2111,2136],"class_list":["post-4390","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-conditionals","lesson-tag-keyboard","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-python","lesson-tag-remote-control","lesson-tag-user-input","module-expert","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4390","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":44,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4390\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13528,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4390\/revisions\/13528"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/10822"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4390"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=4390"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=4390"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}